        <h1 class="post-detail__title">Tin Cup Challenge: Teton Arts</h1>

        <div class="post-detail__featured-image">
          <img src="/assets/images/news/50860.webp" alt="Tin Cup Challenge: Teton Arts" loading="lazy">
        </div>

        <div class="post-detail__content">
          <p><em>&#8220;Teton Arts provides a safe community space for community members of all ages to exercise and explore their creativity. Afterschool programs and summer camp provide crucial childcare in our community while empowering the next generation to explore their imaginations.  Adult classes and workshops offer a great diversity of experiences where adults can find community, make new friends, and benefit from the simple act of creating.  With the support of our community and Tin Cup Funds, we subsidize programs and offer scholarships ensuring that these creative experiences remain affordable and accessible for everyone in Teton Valley. &#8221; &#8211; Greg Meyers, Executive Director</em></p>

<p>At Teton Arts, our ability to keep our programs affordable for everyone in our community is directly related to the support we receive from Tin Cup.&nbsp; Thanks to the annual boost in donor support matched by challenger funds, we can offer art experiences for participants below a price point considered profitable.&nbsp; With this consistent and growing funding source, we are able to offer creative experiences that are specifically suited for seniors, kids, and adults in our community.&nbsp; Tin Cup Funds truly are the foundation of our financial strategy, providing solid support as we grow programming in our pursuit to keep creative experiences affordable as we expand to engage larger portions of our community.&nbsp; Without Tin Cup, we would struggle to provide subsidized art classes and our greatly utilized scholarships.&nbsp; Partnered with our communities’ support through Tin Cup, we joyously work to make creative experiences affordable and accessible for everyone in our community!</p>
